%% CanvasRuntime lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Creating: CanvasRuntime(...)

  state "Creating runtime" as Creating
  note right of Creating
    Initialize committed document, runtime owners,
    public ports, streams, listenables, and caches.
    No legacy SceneController, NodeSpec, or PatchField entities.
  end note

  Creating --> Active: initial committed immutable document is installed

  state "Active runtime" as Active
  note right of Active
    Public mutating operations are admitted through
    runtime boundary guards and owning kernels.
  end note

  Active --> Active: readDocument() / return current immutable document
  Active --> Active: successful edit or command / atomic commit and typed effects
  Active --> Active: loadDocument success / success-only interaction interrupt, atomic replacement, cache invalidation
  Active --> Active: loadDocument failure / no interrupt, no mutation, no repaint, no events
  Active --> Disposing: dispose() first call

  state "Disposing runtime" as Disposing {
    [*] --> EnterGuard
    EnterGuard: enter disposing guard
    EnterGuard --> StopRouting: reject reentrant mutation and new pointer routing
    StopRouting: stop public pointer routing

    StopRouting --> GestureDecision
    state GestureDecision <<choice>>
    GestureDecision --> SelectedMoveCleanup: active selected move preview
    GestureDecision --> OverlayCleanup: active overlay preview
    GestureDecision --> NoGestureCleanup: no active preview

    SelectedMoveCleanup: clear selected move preview and active session
    SelectedMoveCleanup --> MainCleanupRepaint: request main-scene repaint cleanup
    MainCleanupRepaint: repaint main scene without selected move preview
    MainCleanupRepaint --> ResourceCacheCleanup

    OverlayCleanup: clear overlay preview and active session
    OverlayCleanup --> OverlayCleanupRepaint: request overlay repaint cleanup
    OverlayCleanupRepaint: repaint overlay without preview primitives
    OverlayCleanupRepaint --> ResourceCacheCleanup

    NoGestureCleanup: no gesture cleanup effect
    NoGestureCleanup --> ResourceCacheCleanup

    ResourceCacheCleanup: clear mandatory v1 resource caches
    ResourceCacheCleanup --> CloseStreams: drop resolved-image cache entries
    CloseStreams: close actions and textEditRequests streams
    CloseStreams --> [*]
  }

  note right of Disposing
    Dispose never calls the move commit resolver.
    Dispose does not dispose app-owned ui.Image instances
    or the app-owned resource resolver.
  end note

  Disposing --> Disposed: cleanup complete

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  note right of Disposed
    Last committed immutable document remains readable.
    Mutating public operations throw StateError("CanvasRuntime is disposed.").
  end note

  Disposed --> Disposed: dispose() again / return without side effects
  Disposed --> Disposed: readDocument() / return last committed immutable document
  Disposed --> Disposed: mutating public operation or pointer sample / throw StateError

  note left of Disposed
    Negative invariants:
    no committed document mutation from dispose;
    no document revision, selection, spatial index,
    projection cache, or resource descriptor mutation
    due solely to dispose;
    no CanvasActionCommitted event from dispose;
    no CanvasTextEditRequested event from dispose;
    no ValueListenable close claim in v1;
    no document or preview revision bump by dispose itself.
  end note
